{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033799","label":"oil paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033618","label":"paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/object/8543","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8543","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":"455, Catalogue Raisonné","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"catalogue raisonnée number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026061"}],"content":"455","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Corn Dark","type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":{"alternate-title":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: The Metropolitan Museum of Art.","title":"Corn, Dark , No. 1","type":"alternate-title"}],"type":"alternate-title"},"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"Corn – No. 1","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"title":"Corn, Dark","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive.","title":"Corn Dark","type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_post_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_post_1999"}],"content":["Lynes publication lists medium as 'Oil on board'. The Met lists medium as 'Oil on wood fiberboard'. (Source: The Met, 2025)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Inscription fragment in Metropolitan Museum of Art files: \"☆{5star}; An American Place2/An American Place9/Mr. Alfred Stieglitz/489 Park Ave\"(GO, graphite). Metropolitan Museum of Art files indicate, \"The artist says that *Corn Dark* was painted in 1924.\" Whitney Archive indicates, \"July 1949: Miss Bry . . . told me that this picture is now on permanent loan to the Metropolitan Museum from Georgia O'Keeffe as part of that Alfred Stieglitz Coll.\" Either this or cat. no. 454 mentioned in 1934 New York (An American Place) exhibition review in *New York Times* (1934). Reproduced in *The Philadelphia Museum Bulletin* (June 1945). (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. Corn Dark, 1924. Oil on wood fiberboard, 31 3/4 x 11 7/8 inches. Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met). Alfred Stieglitz Collection, 1950. © Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Alfred Stieglitz Collection, 1950","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"31 3/4 x 11 7/8 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Oil on wood fiberboard, 31 3/4 x 11 7/8 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"The artist (1924–50; on extended loan to MMA, 1949–50; her gift as part of the Alfred Stieglitz Collection to MMA) (Source: The Met, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Twisting, dark corn leaves with bright white veins, seen from above, wrap around the center of the composition. A dark red background contrasts with the green corn plant.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on wood fiberboard","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"selected_references","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/selected_references"}],"content":"Edward Alden Jewell. \"Georgia O'Keeffe in an Art Review.\" New York Times (February 2, 1934), p. 15, mentions \"Young Corn,\" 1921 [possibly this work]. \n \nJohn I. H. Baur. Revolution and Tradition in Modern American Art. Cambridge, Mass., 1951, fig. 76. \n \nGeorgia O'Keeffe. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1976, text facing pl. 34, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. \"Georgia O'Keeffe.\" Metropolitan Museum of Art Bulletin 42 (Fall 1984), pp. 19–20, 60, fig. 17, cover ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1988, pp. 33–35, fig. 21. \n \nRoxana Robinson. Georgia O'Keeffe: A Life. New York, 1989, p. 269. \n \nElizabeth Montgomery. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1993, pp. 54–55, ill. \n \nLucy Belloli. \"The Effects of Time: Georgia O'Keeffe's 'Black Hollyhock, Blue Larkspur'.\" Metropolitan Museum of Art Bulletin 51 (Winter 1993–94), pp. 40–41. \n \nRobin Jaffee Frank. Charles Demuth Poster Portraits: 1923–1929. Exh. cat., Yale University Art Gallery. New Haven, 1994, p. 24, fig. 18. \n \nBritta Benke. Georgia O'Keeffe, 1887–1986: Blumen in der Wüste. Cologne, 1994, p. 26, ill. \n \nLowery Stokes Sims in Still Life: The Object in American Art, 1915-1995. Selections from The Metropolitan Museum of Art. Exh. cat., Marsh Art Gallery, Richmond, Va. New York, 1996, pp. 26, 170, no. 1, ill. p. 27 (color). \n \nLowery Stokes Sims and Sabine Rewald in Still Life: The Object in American Art, 1915-1995. Selections from The Metropolitan Museum of Art. Exh. cat., Marsh Art Gallery, Richmond, Va. New York, 1996, p. 18. \n \nLowery Stokes Sims and Sabine Rewald. \"Still Life: The Object in American Art.\" American Art Review 9 (September–October 1997), p. 142, ill. p. 139 (color). \n \nSibella C. Giorello. \"Still Lifes on the Move: The Coming of Age of 'The Neglected Step Child of High Art'.\" Richmond Times-Dispatch (January 19, 1997), p. J1. \n \nJohn Brandenburg. \"Still Lifes Convey Emotion Without Motion.\" Daily Oklahoman (September 26, 1997), p. 13, calls it \"Corn, Dark, I\". \n \nBram Dijkstra. Georgia O'Keeffe and the Eros of Place. Princeton, 1998, p. 216. \n \nDan England. \"Still Life: Metropolitan Museum of Art Exhibit Shows Most Basic of Art Forms Still Has Plenty of Life.\" Salina Journal (March 6, 1998), p. D1, ill. p. D4. \n \nWilliam Jaeger. \"Looking at 'Still Life' is Almost Like Going Home.\" Times Union (June 28, 1998), p. 12. \n \nTimothy Cahill. \"Still Life Moves Up.\" Times Union (May 24, 1998), p. 14, ill. p. 11. \n \nBarbara Buhler Lynes. Georgia O'Keeffe: Catalogue Raisonné. New Haven, Conn., 1999, vol. 1, p. 247, no. 455, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. Georgia O'Keeffe. London, 2001, pp. 67–68, fig. 41. \n \nBarbara Buhler Lynes with Russell Bowman. O'Keeffe's O'Keeffes: The Artist's Collection. Exh. cat., Milwaukee Art Museum. New York, 2001, pp. 50, 169. \n \nPeter R. Kalb. High Drama: The New York Cityscapes of Georgia O'Keeffe and Margaret Bourke-White. New York, 2003, p. iii. \n \nWanda Corn. \"Telling Tales: Georgia O'Keeffe on Georgia O'Keeffe.\" American Art 23 (Summer 2009), pp. 70–71, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger in Stieglitz and His Artists: Matisse to O'Keeffe. The Alfred Stieglitz Collection in The Metropolitan Museum of Art. Ed. Lisa Mintz Messinger. Exh. cat., The Metropolitan Museum of Art. New York, 2011, pp. 14, 198, 278–79, no. 181, ill. (color). \n \nIsabelle Duvernois in Stieglitz and His Artists: Matisse to O'Keeffe. The Alfred Stieglitz Collection in The Metropolitan Museum of Art. Ed. Lisa Mintz Messinger. Exh. cat., The Metropolitan Museum of Art. New York, 2011, p. 193. \n \nBritta Benke. Georgia O'Keeffe, 1887-1986: Flowers in the Desert. Cologne, 2011, p. 26, ill (color). \n \nMarta Ruiz del Árbol. Georgia O'Keeffe. Exh. cat., Museo Nacional Thyssen-Bornemisza. Madrid, 2021, pp. 33, 309, no. 34, ill. (color) and ill. p. 144 (color). \n \nAnnelise K. Madsen in Georgia O'Keeffe: \"My New Yorks\". Ed. Sarah Kelly Oehler and Annelise K. Madsen. Exh. cat., Art Institute of Chicago. Chicago, 2024, pp. 40, 200, colorpl. 7.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"Corn Dark, 1924","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/884913/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/884913"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}